@3rd-Eden 

> And comments are ever an excuse for sloppy code.

A counter example from the current node codebase ([link](https://github.com/joyent/node/blob/cfcb1de130867197cbc9c6012b7e84e08e53d032/lib/_stream_readable.js#L160-L163)):

``` js
// if we want the data now, just emit it.
if (state.flowing && state.length === 0 && !state.sync) {
  stream.emit('data', chunk);
  stream.read(0);
} else {
  // ...
}
```

Rewritten so that no comment is needed:

``` js
var dataWantedNow = state.flowing && state.length === 0 &&  !state.sync;
if (dataWantedNow) {
  stream.emit('data', chunk);
  stream.read(0);
} else {
  // ...
}
```

